{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/621116-pack-tactics-in-2ed","id":621116,"title":"Pack Tactics in 2ed","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-09T05:59:52-07:00","id":621116,"title":"Pack Tactics in 2ed","content":"Did I miss something or pack tactics are gone again in 2ed? I'm preparing for new chronicle, where I want to put an emphasis on teamwork and cooperation so pack tactics would be nice addition. Still I can't find them anywhere in the Corebook.Are they gone? If so are there any clues as to their return. Or perhaps someone could share his/her homebrew ideas for how pack tactics could work now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2637-qendi","name":"qendi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-09T06:04:28-07:00","id":621138,"title":"","content":"There's the Pack Bond Merit, which gives you a bonus on teamwork actions with your packmates.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-09T08:00:50-07:00","id":621259,"title":"","content":"Plus, like, a dozen or so gift facets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-09T08:01:38-07:00","id":621261,"title":"","content":"There are some gifts that work well when you have your pack with you, such as Pack Triumphs Together (from the Gifts of Inspiration), Pack Stalks the Prey (from the Gifts of Stealth) and Reflected Facets (from the Gifts of Pack), to name a few. But no real pack tactics as yet. I'm hoping the upcoming The Pack sourcebook is going to cover things like pack tactics in more detail than what we've had in the past. With the addition of non-werewolves in the packs, I think there's a lot more that can be done with pack tactics now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7226-cloud-dreamer","name":"Cloud Dreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-09T08:21:06-07:00","id":621296,"title":"","content":"Frankly, I think you can do the job with the rules for tactics found in Hunter: The Vigil.<br /> <br /> They're not usually meant for supernaturals on the assumption that they don't need an even greater edge, but you can implement them for the effect quite easily.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-09T08:26:52-07:00","id":621306,"title":"","content":"I sought to fold a lot of pack-based capabilities into the Gifts, making teamwork and working off other packmates a more core concept right in the mechanics. I have to admit that I never really liked the 1e pack tactics rules very much; my players rarely got much meaningful use out of them. They were a nice idea but I wasn't convinced by the implementation they received.<br /> <br /> If pack tactics reappear in 2e then I expect they'll get a pretty thorough reworking to fit into the new system and make them awesome.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/621116-pack-tactics-in-2ed?p=621296#post621296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Frankly, I think you can do the job with the rules for tactics found in Hunter: The Vigil.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those pretty much are the same rules as the pack tactics rules from 1e Werewolf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-09T08:32:20-07:00","id":621336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/621116-pack-tactics-in-2ed?p=621306#post621306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If pack tactics reappear in 2e then I expect they'll get a pretty thorough reworking to fit into the new system and make them awesome.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Does this mean that pack tactics will not be in The Pack?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3669-blackheartz","name":"blackheartz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3669_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-09T08:35:08-07:00","id":621340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>qendi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/621116-pack-tactics-in-2ed#post621116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did I miss something or pack tactics are gone again in 2ed? I'm preparing for new chronicle, where I want to put an emphasis on teamwork and cooperation so pack tactics would be nice addition. Still I can't find them anywhere in the Corebook.Are they gone? If so are there any clues as to their return. Or perhaps someone could share his/her homebrew ideas for how pack tactics could work now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not as much &quot;gone again&quot; as &quot;not yet reintroduced&quot;. Even though Werewolf was a small line, lots of books, and thus rules, have been produced. Not everything can fit into a core book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-09T09:17:08-07:00","id":621393,"title":"","content":"What would Pack Tactics do that Pack Dynamics, Creative Tactician and the right powers don't already do?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-09T09:23:33-07:00","id":621399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackheartz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/621116-pack-tactics-in-2ed?p=621336#post621336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Does this mean that pack tactics will not be in The Pack?</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't reveal what is and is not in The Pack at this time - that's up to Stew.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-09T14:41:03-07:00","id":621632,"title":"","content":"Frankly, I would let Pack Tactics out of The Pack and put some better rules for team tactics on the new nWoD core book. I know they are in theme with Werewolf because of the Pack, but in truth this kind of rule should be useful for any group.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T02:58:22-07:00","id":621993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/621116-pack-tactics-in-2ed?p=621632#post621632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Frankly, I would let Pack Tactics out of The Pack and put some better rules for team tactics on the new nWoD core book. I know they are in theme with Werewolf because of the Pack, but in truth this kind of rule should be useful for any group.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is not possible to do in the nWoD corebook. In another blue supplement maybe. With that being said I do not believe that pack tactics are even needed in this edition. The purpose of my previous post was more sinister <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3669-blackheartz","name":"blackheartz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3669_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}